<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="31720dcb-1fee-5aa7-8502-6ffd81659f94" activityNameId="84eebe81-8678-5521-8bf0-5c387b3d5133" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sweetening, natural gas</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sweetening, natural gas
Data is based on the environmental report of the plant of Grossenkneten.;
UUID: fc55c031-edef-3c41-aa8a-65564aedf9df
Sweetening of sour gas with average 10 Vol.-% of H2S. The data refers to 1 m3 output gas
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The data is taken out the BEB environmental report 2000. The plant in Grossenkneten is operational since 1972 and is according to BEB one of the biggest and environmental friendliest of the world. It eliminates sulphur compounds to 99.99% from gas. The connected sulphur extraction plant has an extraction rate of 99.8%. The production in Grossenkneten is 4.8 Mrd. m3 gas per year. Sour gas with less as 1% H2S (lean gas) is treated with the Purisol process (physically), sour gas with more sulphur is treated chemically. The solutions used for the gas scrubbing are regenerated and warmed up to 130 °C. By this process a gas mix of H2S and CO2 is released. Subsequently H2S is transformed in elementary sulphur and water in a thermal process by 1"000-2"000°C and in a three-stage catalytic part.
Time period: Average of 5 last years is used (1996-2000). Emissions per m3 were stable. 
Production volume: 4.8E9 Sm3 natural gas, 0.7 E9 kg Sulphur
Sampling: Data is based on environmental report. No information about the sampling procedure. 
Extrapolations: Data for Germany are extrapolated out of the data for the sweetening plant Grossenkneten.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fc55c031-edef-3c41-aa8a-65564aedf9df.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="948c6fdb-25b0-54ae-bf5c-e320176f724c" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
